{'symbol': 'PFE', 'date': '2021-09-30 06:45:00', 'title': "JAPAN'S MHLW APPROVES PFIZER'S CIBINQO® (ABROCITINIB) FOR ADULTS AND ADOLESCENTS WITH MODERATE TO SEVERE ATOPIC DERMATITIS", 'text': 'NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--PFIZER INC. (NYSE: PFE) TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT THE JAPANESE MINISTRY OF HEALTH, LABOUR AND WELFARE (MHLW) HAS APPROVED CIBINQO® (ABROCITINIB), AN ORAL, ONCE-DAILY, JANUS KINASE 1 (JAK1) INHIBITOR, FOR THE TREATMENT OF MODERATE TO SEVERE ATOPIC DERMATITIS (AD) IN ADULTS AND ADOLESCENTS AGED 12 YEARS AND OLDER WITH INADEQUATE RESPONSE TO EXISTING THERAPIES. CIBINQO WILL BE AVAILABLE IN JAPAN IN DOSES OF 100MG AND 200MG. “THERE HAVE BEEN LIMITED TREATMENT OPTIONS AVAILABLE'}